<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Chromite bundled JDBC drivers of the major databases (docs/chromite/drivers.md).

    Design: the product bundle declarations (com.seizia.chromite.drivers.public) and the drivers/ root files
    (jars fetched by pom.xml, license texts from drivers-root/) must always ship together: a declared bundle
    without its folder leaves the driver without any file source. Keeping both in one feature makes that the
    unit of inclusion: a product feature (com.seizia.chromite.swing.feature) includes it and gets the drivers
    from a single jar list.
    p2 installs a feature's root files with the feature itself, also when it is only included by another feature.

    History:
    - 2026-11-06 Created. Moved out of com.seizia.chromite.ce.feature so the Swing product ships the same drivers.
    - 2026-11-07 The SWT product was removed (docs/chromite/swt-removal.md); the Swing feature is the only includer.
    - 2026-11-07 Added SQLite. Chromite ships one edition (no internal edition), so the "public edition" labels
      became "bundled drivers"; the feature and plugin IDs keep "public" because renaming them buys nothing.
    - 2026-11-07 Removed MySQL Connector/J (user decision); MySQL drivers download it when first used.
    - 2026-11-14 Added ShardSphere (project owner's decision). Its jar is not on Maven Central, so it is committed in
      drivers-root/drivers/shardsphere/ and reaches drivers/ as a root file like the license texts.
-->
<feature
        id="com.seizia.chromite.drivers.public.feature"
        label="Chromite Bundled JDBC Drivers"
        version="26.2.5.qualifier"
        provider-name="Chromite contributors">

    <description>JDBC drivers bundled with Chromite: SQL Server, Oracle, PostgreSQL, MariaDB, SQLite, ShardSphere</description>

    <copyright>Chromite contributors. Driver licenses: drivers/README.txt</copyright>

    <!-- Declares the bundled driver folders that pom.xml puts into the root files (drivers/) -->
    <plugin id="com.seizia.chromite.drivers.public" version="0.0.0"/>

</feature>
